# Change Log

## 4.1.0

### Added

- Added the AI project API in `api/Rooms/`: `AIApi` with `getProjectModel` and `setProjectModel` (the chat model of an AI project), `getProjectSources`, `linkProjectSources` and `unlinkProjectSources` (the rooms linked to a project as its sources), `getRoomSkills` and `getRoomsSkills` (the skills of an Instructions room and the skills catalog), with the models `AiProjectModel`, `AiProjectModelDto`, `AiProjectModelWrapper`, `AiProjectSourceDto`, `AiProjectSourcesDto`, `AiProjectSourcesWrapper`, `AiSkillDto`, `AiSkillsDto`, `AiSkillsRoomDto`, `AiSkillsWrapper`, `LinkAiProjectSourcesRequest`, `UnlinkAiProjectSourcesRequest` and `UpdateAiProjectModelRequest`
- Added `aiContextGetKnowledgeFolders` to the AI `ContextApi`
- `aiAssignmentsGetAllAssignments` takes `expand`: `profile` answers the assigned profiles themselves instead of their IDs
- Added `hasMetadataFields` to `EntryMetadataDto`
- Added enum values: `RoomType.InstructionsRoom`, `KnowledgeRoom` and `AiProjectRoom`; `FolderType.InstructionsRoom`, `KnowledgeRoom`, `AiProjectRoom` and `AiHub`; `FilterType.InstructionsRooms`, `KnowledgeRooms` and `AiProjectRooms`; `SearchArea.AiHub`; `SubjectType.AiProject`; `MessageAction.RoomsLinkedToAiProject`, `RoomsUnlinkedFromAiProject` and `AiProjectProfileAssigned`
- The chat-service answers that were declared as a bare `{ success }` are typed: `attachments/suggested-questions` returns `AiSuggestedQuestionsResult` (`status` and `questions` of `AiSuggestedQuestion`), `context/get-context-folders` and `context/get-knowledge-folders` a list of `AiContextFolder`, `context/get-room-skills` a list of `AiRoomSkill`, `context/get-room-skill` the skill text, and `settings/config/tool-mode` (read and write) `AiToolPermissionModeWrapper`
- Request fields the chat service already read: `AiActionArgs` gains `contextRooms` (`AiContextRoomRef`), `knowledgeRooms` (`AiKnowledgeRoomRef`), `folderContext` (`AiFolderContextRef`), `toolInstructions` and `entityId` (`knowledgeRoom` is deprecated); `contextEntityId` is added to `AiSendRequest`, `AiSendStreamBody`, `AiRegenerateStreamRequest` and `AiToolCallData`, `profileId` to `AiSendCustomRequest`, `messageId`, `keepCount` and `expectedLength` to `AiRegenerateStreamRequest`, and `format` (`Docx`, `Pdf` or `Md`) to `AiExportTextToDocxRequest`
- `AiThreadMessageLike` describes what is stored: `status` carries `reason` and `error` (`AiChatErrorPayload`), and the content parts carry the tool-call fields (`toolName`, `toolCallId`, `args`, `result`) and the file fields (`mimeType`, `data`, `image`, `name`, `filename`)

### Changed

- `threads/append-user-message` answers `messageId` as the stored message (`AiThreadMessageLike`, its ID in `messageId.id`) - the service always sent it so, the SDK declared a string
- `assignments/get-all-assignments` answers one of two shapes: the map of action to profile ID, or with `expand=profile` `AiAssignmentsExpanded` (`assignments`, `profilesTotal`, `chatProfilesTotal`)
- `attachments/suggested-questions` takes the attachment ID itself as the body (a string) instead of an object
- `AiPromptBundle.version` is an integer, so `prompts/import-bundle` accepts a bundle exported through the SDK (the version used to be sent as the string "1" and the import refused it)
- The inline models of `FileEntryDto` lost their `Ai` prefix: `AiFileEntryDtoAllOfAvailableShareRights`, `AiFileEntryDtoAllOfSecurity` and `AiFileEntryDtoAllOfShareSettings` are now `FileEntryDtoAllOfAvailableShareRights`, `FileEntryDtoAllOfSecurity` and `FileEntryDtoAllOfShareSettings`
- The API version is 4.1.0

### Removed

- Removed the AI agents: `AgentsApi` in `api/AI/` (`aiAgentsList`, `aiAgentsCreate`, `aiAgentsGet`, `aiAgentsUpdate`, `aiAgentsDelete`, `aiAgentsNews`, `aiAgentsUpdateQuota` and `aiAgentsResetQuota`) and the `Ai`-prefixed models it used (`AiFolderWrapper`, `AiFolderContentWrapper`, `AiFileOperationWrapper`, `AiAgentsCreateRequest`, `AiAgentsUpdateRequest` and the others). The server no longer serves `/api/2.0/ai/agents`; an AI project (`RoomType.AiProjectRoom`) takes the place of an agent

## 4.0.0

### Added

- Third-party storage support: 100 operations that address a file, folder or room (for example `getFileInfo`, `getFolderByFolderId`, `updateRoom`, `uploadFile`, the sharing and upload-session operations) have an overload that takes the string identifier of an entry in a connected third-party storage (for example `"sbox-42"`) and returns the matching `ThirdParty*` model (`ThirdPartyFileWrapper`, `ThirdPartyFolderWrapper`, `ThirdPartyFolderContentWrapper`, `ThirdPartyChunkedUploadSessionWrapper` and others); the string overloads of `saveFileAsPdf` and `startFileConversion` take `ThirdPartySaveAsPdfRequest` and `ThirdPartyCheckConversionRequestDto`
- Added the reworked AI API in `api/AI/`: `AIApi` (sending messages with or without streaming, regenerating answers, approving and denying tool calls), `AssignmentsApi`, `AttachmentsApi`, `ContextApi`, `EditorToolsApi`, `ExportApi`, `OpenAIPassthroughApi`, `PreferencesApi`, `ProfilesApi`, `PromptsApi`, `ThreadsApi`, `ToolsApi` and `WebSearchApi`; the AI `SettingsApi` gains `aiSettingsGetToolMode` and `aiSettingsSetToolMode`
- Added `MetadataApi` (`api/Files/`): metadata templates and their fields, assigning templates to files and folders, custom fields and field values; the new `searchFolder` and `searchRooms` find entries by their metadata, and files and folders carry `assignedMetadataTemplates` and `metadataMatches`
- Added `AppsApi` (`api/Apps/`), `PrivacyRoomApi` (`api/Rooms/`, the users' encryption keys for privacy rooms) and `DocsCloudApi` (`api/Settings/`)
- Added the Files operations `getFormsFolder`, `getRoomAiFolder`, `showQuickActions`, `getEncryptionInfo`, `setEncryptionInfo` and `getEncryptionAccess`
- Report generation: `createReportFolderHistory`, `createAuditTrailReport` and `createLoginHistoryReport` take `format`, `from` and `to` and return a `DocumentBuilderTaskWrapper`; the new `getReportFolderHistory`, `getAuditTrailReport`, `getLoginHistoryReport` and the matching `terminate*` operations follow and cancel the report
- Added the payment operations `getActiveServices`, `getAccountingServicePrices`, `getSubscriptionBalanceInfo`, `moveSubscriptionToWallet`, `getCustomerServiceUsage` and `getCustomerMonthlyUsage` with their `create*Report`, `get*Report` and `terminate*Report` operations, and `getUpcomingPayments` in `QuotaApi` (`api/Portal/`)
- Added `getBackupsCounts` (`BackupApi`) and `refreshWebPlugin` (`WebpluginsApi`)
- Added model properties: `showQuickActions` to `FilesSettingsDto`, `formsUsedSpace` to `FilesStatisticsResultDto`, `ai` to `CustomizationConfigDto`, `isDelayedPaymentMethod` and `paymentMethodType` to `CustomerInfoDto`, `searchArea` to `RoomGroupDto` and `RoomGroupRequestDto`, `walletLowBalance` to `SettingsDto`, `runtime` to `WebPluginDto`, `toolPermissionMode` to `AiSettingsDto` and `AiUserSettingsDto`, `lastModified` to `TenantAiAccessSettingsDto`, `TenantBannerSettingsDto` and `TenantDevToolsAccessSettingsDto`, `errors` to `ProblemDetail`; `OperationDto` describes the source of a charge with `sourceId`, `sourceTitle`, `sourceType`, `cost` and `tokenUsage` instead of `agentId` and `agentTitle`
- Added enum values: `FolderType.Forms` and `FolderType.Ai`; `TenantWalletService.Admin`, `DocsCloud`, `DocsCloudDevPack` and `AISearch`; new audit actions in `MessageAction`
- Added the error body models `ErrorApiResponse` and `ValidationErrorResponse` (with `FieldError`)

### Changed

- Files, folders and rooms use one set of models for numeric identifiers: the `Integer` suffix is gone (`FileIntegerWrapper` → `FileWrapper`, `FolderIntegerWrapper` → `FolderWrapper`, `FolderContentIntegerWrapper` → `FolderContentWrapper`, `FileDtoInteger` → `FileDto`, `FolderDtoInteger` → `FolderDto`, `ConfigurationIntegerWrapper` → `ConfigurationWrapper`, `UploadSessionResponseIntegerWrapper` → `UploadSessionResponseWrapper`, `OrdersRequestDtoInteger` → `OrdersRequestDto`, `UpdateRoomsQuotaRequestDtoInteger` → `UpdateRoomsQuotaRequestDto`, `SaveAsPdfInteger` → `SaveAsPdfRequest` and so on), and the `String` variants became `ThirdParty*` models (`FolderStringWrapper` → `ThirdPartyFolderWrapper`, `FolderDtoString` → `ThirdPartyFolderDto`, `FileEntryDtoString` → `ThirdPartyFileEntryDto`); the chunked-upload operations return `ChunkedUploadSessionWrapper` and `ChunkedUploadSessionResultWrapper`
- Renamed the request models with the plural `Requests` to the singular (`AuthRequestsDto` → `AuthRequestDto`, `SsoSettingsRequestsDto` → `SsoSettingsRequestDto`, `TfaRequestsDto` → `TfaRequestDto`, `StorageRequestsDto` → `StorageRequestDto`, `CspRequestsDto` → `CspRequestDto`, `WhiteLabelRequestsDto` → `WhiteLabelRequestDto`, `WebPluginRequests` → `WebPluginRequest` and the rest), and the JSON bodies nested in a request take a `Request` suffix (`Delete` → `DeleteFileRequest`, `DeleteFolder` → `DeleteFolderRequest`, `CreateFolder` → `CreateFolderRequest`, `CreateFileJsonElement` → `CreateFileRequest`, `CreateTextOrHtmlFile` → `CreateTextOrHtmlFileRequest`, `CopyAsJsonElement` → `CopyAsRequest`, `UpdateFile` → `UpdateFileRequest`, `UpdateComment` → `UpdateCommentRequest`, `ChangeHistory` → `ChangeHistoryRequest`, `CheckFillFormDraft` → `CheckFillFormDraftRequest`, `CustomFilterParameters` → `CustomFilterRequest`, `CreateThirdPartyRoom` → `CreateThirdPartyRoomRequest`, `LockFileParameters` → `LockFileRequest`, `StartEdit` → `StartEditRequest`, `Culture` → `UpdateMemberCultureRequest`, `MentionMessageWrapper` → `MentionMessageRequest`, `EmailValidationKeyModel` → `CheckConfirmRequestDto`); the JSON sent is unchanged
- Settings, database entities and other server-side classes are no longer published as models: each one became a `Dto` of the same shape (`TenantQuota` → `TenantQuotaDto`, `Balance` → `BalanceDto`, `Tariff` → `TariffDto`, `BackupProgress` → `BackupProgressDto`, `CoEditingConfig` → `CoEditingConfigDto`, `Logo` → `LogoDto`, `StorageSettings` → `StorageSettingsDto`, `DarkThemeSettings` → `DarkThemeSettingsDto`, `WizardSettings` → `WizardSettingsDto` and so on) or a model named after what it carries (`UserInfo` → `PortalUserDto`, also as the `user` of `MentionDto`, `FireBaseUser` → `FirebaseDeviceDto`, `ThirdPartyParams` → `ThirdPartyAccountDto`, `CompanyWhiteLabelSettings` → `LicensorDetailsDto`, `AdditionalWhiteLabelSettings` → `AdditionalResourcesDto`, `SsoSettingsV2` → `SsoSettingsDto`, `IPRestriction` → `IpRestrictionDto`, `SetupCode` → `TfaSetupCodeDto`); the room, user and AI agent quota settings are all returned as `EntityQuotaSettingsWrapper`
- The settings sent in a request body take the name of their operation and keep every field (`TenantWalletSettingsWrapper` → `TenantWalletSettingsRequestDto` with `SetWalletTopUpSettingsRequest`, `TenantAuditSettingsWrapper` → `TenantAuditSettingsRequestDto` with `SetAuditLifetimeSettingsRequest`, `CompanyWhiteLabelSettingsWrapper` → `CompanyWhiteLabelSettingsRequestDto` with `SaveCompanyInfoRequest`, `AdditionalWhiteLabelSettingsWrapper` → `AdditionalWhiteLabelSettingsRequestDto` with `SaveAdditionalResourcesRequest`, `TenantAiAccessSettingsDto` → `TenantAiAccessSettingsRequestDto`, `TenantBannerSettingsDto` → `TenantBannerSettingsRequestDto`, `TenantDevToolsAccessSettingsDto` → `TenantDevToolsAccessSettingsRequestDto`, `ExternalDatabaseSettings` → `ExternalDatabaseConnectionRequestDto`, `EmailActivationSettings` → `EmailActivationSettingsRequestDto`); `TenantWalletSettingsWrapper`, `TenantAuditSettingsWrapper`, `CompanyWhiteLabelSettingsWrapper` and `AdditionalWhiteLabelSettingsWrapper` return the settings in `response` instead of a `settings` property; `saveAuthKeys` takes `SaveAuthKeysRequestDto` and `getAuthServices` returns `AuthServiceArrayWrapper`
- Renamed other models whose names did not say what they carry: `Status` → `ExternalShareStatus`, `Options` → `DocumentOptionsDto`, `STRINGArrayWrapper` → `StringArrayWrapper`, `EncryprtionStatus` → `EncryptionStatus`, `AceShortWrapper` → `AceShortDto`, `MentionWrapper` → `MentionDto`, `TimezonesRequestsDto` → `TimezoneDto`, `GroupMemberSecurityRequestDto` → `GroupMemberSecurityDto`, `SmtpOperationStatusRequestsDto` → `SmtpOperationStatusDto`, `KeyValuePairBooleanString` → `ItemKeyValuePairBooleanString`, `HistoryData` → `HistoryDataDto`, `HistoryAction` → `HistoryActionDto`, `Area` → `AccountSearchArea`, `Location` → `RequestLocation`, `TfaRequestsDtoType` → `TfaType`, and the backup request models after their operation (`BackupDto` → `StartBackupRequestDto`, `BackupRestoreDto` → `StartBackupRestoreRequestDto`, `BackupScheduleDto` → `CreateBackupScheduleRequestDto`, `Cron` → `BackupCronRequest`)
- Operations that returned an untyped `ObjectWrapper` or `ObjectArrayWrapper` now return a typed model: `StringWrapper` (`getPortalPath`, `getPortalHostname`, `getGreetingSettings`, `getThirdPartyCode`), `StringArrayWrapper` (`getRoomTagsInfo`), `TokenDiagnosticsWrapper` (`getClaims`), `AuditTrailProductArrayWrapper` (`getAuditTrailMappers`), `AuditTrailTypesWrapper` (`getAuditTrailTypes`), `EnabledModuleArrayWrapper` (`getEnabledModules`), `SocketSettingsWrapper` (`getSocketSettings`), `SsoSettingsConstantsWrapper` (`getSsoSettingsV2Constants`), `AmazonS3RegionArrayWrapper` (`getAmazonS3Regions`), `AccountEntryArrayWrapper` (`getAccountsEntriesWith*Shared`)
- Other return types: `deleteFileVersions` returns `FileOperationArrayWrapper`, `searchUsersByQuery` returns `EmployeeFullArrayWrapper`, `changeDefaultAccessRights` returns `FileShareResponseArrayWrapper`, `updateCdnStorage` returns `StorageSettingsWrapper`, `getAiPrices` returns `AiPricesWrapper`, `getRestrictedAiModels` and `setRestrictedAiModels` return `RestrictedAiModelsWrapper`; `deleteGroup` and `deleteRecent` return `void`
- Renamed the AI operations after their tag, so the method names change: `createAgent` → `aiAgentsCreate`, `getAgents` → `aiAgentsList`, `getAgentInfo` → `aiAgentsGet`, `getAgentsNewItems` → `aiAgentsNews`, `updateAgent` → `aiAgentsUpdate`, `deleteAgent` → `aiAgentsDelete`, `updateAgentsQuota` → `aiAgentsUpdateQuota`, `resetAgentsQuota` → `aiAgentsResetQuota`, `getAiSettings` → `aiSettingsGet`, `getAiUserSettings` → `aiSettingsGetUser`, `setAiUserSettings` → `aiSettingsSetUser`, `getVectorizationSettings` → `aiSettingsGetVectorization`, `setVectorizationSettings` → `aiSettingsSetVectorization`, `startTask` → `aiVectorizationStartTask`; in Files, `changeDownloadZipFromBody` → `changeDownloadZip`
- The AI agent operations take the agent `id` as a `String` and use their own `Ai`-prefixed models (`AiFolderWrapper`, `AiFolderContentWrapper`, `AiFileOperationWrapper`, `AiAgentsCreateRequest`, `AiAgentsUpdateRequest` and others) instead of the models of the Files API; `aiAgentsList` takes its filters in a new order, with `quotaFilter` as an `Integer` and `sortOrder` as a `String`; `aiSettingsSetUser` and `aiSettingsSetVectorization` take the settings as a `Map<String, Object>`
- The AI operations authenticate with the new `cookieAuth` and `bearerAuth` schemes, and `ApiClient.setBearerToken` sets the token on every bearer scheme instead of only the first one, so a single call authorizes both the AI and the other operations
- The OAuth 2.0 client and scope operations call `/api/2.0/oauth2/clients` and `/api/2.0/oauth2/scopes` instead of `/api/2.0/clients` and `/api/2.0/scopes`; `getClients` returns `PageableClientResponse` instead of `PageableResponse`, `getClientsInfo` returns `PageableClientInfoResponse` (renamed from `PageableResponseClientInfoResponse`), `getScopes` returns `List<ScopeResponse>` instead of one `ScopeResponse`, and `changeActivation`, `deleteClient`, `deleteTenantClients`, `deleteUserClients`, `revokeUserClient`, `updateClient` and `handleOptions` return `void` instead of `Object`; `UpdateClientRequest` takes `redirect_uris` and `scopes`
- `checkMoveOrCopyBatchItems` and `checkMoveOrCopyDestFolder` take the batch as separate parameters (`returnSingleOperation`, `folderIds`, `fileIds`, `destFolderId`, `conflictResolveType`, `deleteAfter`, `content`, `toFillOut`) instead of one `inDto` object, which is how the server reads them
- New and changed method parameters (positional, so existing calls must be updated): the folder listings `getMyFolder`, `getFavoritesFolder`, `getRecentFolder`, `getTrashFolder`, `getFolderByFolderId` and `getRoomsFolder` take two new trailing parameters `metadataTemplateId` and `metadataFilters`; `getFolderByFolderId` also takes `folderType` after `roomId`, and its `location` is a `RequestLocation`; `getRoomsFolder` no longer takes `subjectFilter`, takes `privacyFilter` and `withAiFolder` before `count`, and its `subjectId` and `subjectOwnerId` are `UUID`; `emptyTrash` takes `folderType`, `getPaymentQuotas` takes `additional`, and `getRoomGroups` takes `searchArea` instead of `id`
- Parameter types: the date filters of `getFileHistory`, `getFolderHistory`, `getAuditEventsByFilter` and `getLoginEventsByFilter` are `OffsetDateTime` instead of `ApiDateTime`; `serviceName` of `getCustomerOperations` and of `CustomerOperationsReportRequestDto` is a `List<String>`; `EditorConfigurationDto.encryptionKeys` is a `List<EncryptionKeyDto>` instead of `EncryptionKeysConfig`
- `SearchArea` is sent and received as a string (`"Active"`, `"Archive"`, ...) instead of a number, and its constants are upper-case (`SearchArea.Active` → `SearchArea.ACTIVE`, `SearchArea.RecentByLinks` → `SearchArea.RECENT_BY_LINKS`); `FolderType.ResultStorage` (33) is now `FolderType.ChatOutputs`

### Removed

- Removed the superseded AI API classes `ChatApi`, `MCPApi`, `MessagesApi` and `ProvidersApi` from `api/AI/` together with their models (`ChatDto`, `MessageDto`, `McpServerDto`, `AiProviderDto`, `ModelDto` and others); the web search settings moved from `getWebSearchSettings`/`setWebSearchSettings` to `WebSearchApi`
- Removed the request models `SetAiUserSettingsRequestDto` and `SetEmbeddingConfigRequestBody`, the `AiSettingsDto` properties that described the old AI chat (`webSearchEnabled`, `portalMcpServerId`, `modelAliases`, the `*ToolName` properties and others) and the model properties of `ChatSettingsDto` (`providerId`, `modelId`, `modelAlias`, `capabilities`, `multimodal`, `thinking`, `internal`)
- Removed `getPrivacyFolder` and `isAvailablePrivacyRoomSettings` (Files), `getCustomerAiBalance` and `creditAiBalance` (Payment)
- Removed the `subjectFilter` parameter of `getRoomsFolder` and `aiAgentsList` with its `SubjectFilter` enum, the `MessageAction` values `PrivacyRoomEnable` and `PrivacyRoomDisable`, and the `public` property of the OAuth 2.0 client models
- Removed the server-side models that no operation uses any more: `DbTenant`, `DbTenantPartner`, `AuthData`, `OAuth20Token`, `NoContentResult`, `NoContentResultWrapper` and `StatusCodeResult`
- The third-party accounts returned by `getThirdPartyAccounts` no longer have the `auth_data` property, and the devices returned by `docRegisterPusnNotificationDevice` and `subscribeDocumentsPushNotification` no longer have `tenant`; neither was ever filled in

## 3.7.0

### Added

- Added new API methods for AI settings, wallet/payment operations, room external sharing & DB sync, file uploads, and webhook triggers
- Added corresponding request/response models (DTOs and wrappers)
- Added rate limit documentation (`X-RateLimit-*` and `Retry-After` headers) to API docs
- Added tag Rooms / Groups

### Changed

- Updated SDK OpenAPI specification to v3.7.0
- Adjusted method return types and renamed several payment/TFA methods
- Updated example values and added email length validation in API models

### Fixed

- Fixed & / ' issues

## 3.6.0

- Initial release
- SDK regenerated from OpenAPI specification v3.6.0